  "C5_population_invariant": {
   "lemma": "P'(a) = P'(b) = (P(a) + P(b))/2 for an event on seam (a,b) (load conserved, active load to |p>); rotations permute ports. The tracial code has P(port occupied) = 1/6 for every port (each port in one pair of every matching), so after any sequence of native seam events and rotations every port still has occupation 1/6 and the unconditional source polarization P(a occupied) - P(b occupied) of any later event is 0.",
